"""AHA PREVENT coefficient tables — all 100 published coefficient sets.

Equation source
---------------
Khan SS, Matsushita K, Sang Y, et al. "Development and Validation of the
American Heart Association's PREVENT Equations." Circulation. 2024;149(6):430-449.
doi:10.1161/CIRCULATIONAHA.123.067626 -- supplemental appendix coefficient tables.

Values transcribed from the MIT-licensed CRAN package `preventr`
(Martin Mayer, https://github.com/martingmayer/preventr, `R/sysdata.rda`), whose
tables are validated against supplemental Table S25 of the development article.
Cross-checked here by reproducing that vignette (see tests/parity/).

Coverage: 5 model variants x 2 horizons x 5 outcomes x 2 sexes = 100 sets.

  variant  extra predictors beyond the base model
  -------  ---------------------------------------------------
  base     none
  uacr     urine albumin-to-creatinine ratio (ln-transformed)
  hba1c    HbA1c, with separate slopes for diabetes / no diabetes
  sdi      social deprivation index decile categories
  full     UACR + HbA1c + SDI together

  horizon  10 (ages 30-79) or 30 (ages 30-59; adds an age-squared term)

Each variant carries a "missing" indicator term for its optional predictor, so a
patient without the extra lab is scored by setting the indicator rather than by
falling back to the base model. That is the published design, not our invention.

Licensing note
--------------
These coefficients are published in a peer-reviewed article and redistributed
under the MIT license on CRAN. AHA's terms cover its own hosted calculator and
branding, not the published equations.
"""

